(Step 12: assign_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(Step 13: activate_destination_node destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 14: lock_destination_availability destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(Now we have both availabilities locked and confirmed, nodes ready.)
(Now assemble transport leg.)
(Step 15: assemble_transport_leg origin_availability_alpha destination_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha destination_node_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(Preconditions: origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available.)
(We have all: origin_availability_locked from step7, destination_availability_locked from step14, node links from init, origin_node_ready from step6, destination_node_ready from step13, origin_availability_confirmed from step7, destination_availability_confirmed from step14, transport_leg_available from init.)
(Effect: transport_leg_assembled, origin_leg_linked, destination_leg_linked, not transport_leg_available.)
(Now authorize transport leg loading.)
(Step 16: authorize_transport_leg_loading transport_leg_alpha origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Precondition: transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked (origin_availability_alpha), not transport_leg_loading_authorized.)
(We have transport_leg_assembled true, origin_availability_locked true, candidate_task_profile_linked true (we attached earlier), not transport_leg_loading_authorized true (init false). So ok.)
(Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized.)
(Now we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized.)
(Now we need to process schedule candidate alpha.)
(We'll need to allocate vehicle, attach task profile, etc. However note that we already used vehicle_unit_alpha for origin availability and vehicle_unit_beta for destination availability. They are now dispatched? Not yet; we haven't dispatched them. We'll need to dispatch them later. But we can still allocate vehicles to schedule candidates after we dispatch the availabilities and release vehicles.)
(Thus we need to dispatch origin and destination availabilities before we can reuse their vehicles for schedule candidates.)
(Thus after we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized, we should mark origin and destination dispatch ready, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch, which will make vehicles available again.)
(Thus we need to do:)
(- mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(- execute_origin_dispatch origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha)
(Similarly for destination.)
(But note: execute_origin_dispatch requires candidate_vehicle_linked (we have from allocate_vehicle_unit), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked (from allocate dispatch slot), and not dispatched.)
(Thus we need to allocate dispatch slot before executing.)
(Thus sequence for origin:)
(Step 15: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(Step 16: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 17: execute_origin_dispatch origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha)
(After this, origin_availability_alpha is dispatched, vehicle_unit_alpha becomes available, dispatch_slot_alpha becomes available.)
(Now we need to do same for destination.)
(Step 18: mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(Step 19: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate destination_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 20: execute_destination_dispatch destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta dispatch_slot_alpha)
(After this, destination_availability_alpha dispatched, vehicle_unit_beta available, dispatch_slot_alpha available.)
(Now we have both availabilities dispatched, vehicles free.)
(Now we can process schedule candidates.)
(We need to ensure we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized (still true). The loading authorized remains true unless we have an action to unset it; none.)
(Now we need to process shift_candidate_alpha.)
(We'll need to allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness, assign operator, assign skill cert, assign compliance cert, load container, stage, verify loading, establish clearance, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch.)
(We need to ensure we have operator available (we released after locking? Actually we assigned operator to origin and destination availabilities via assign_operator_resource. After locking, we still have operator linked to those availabilities. We haven't released them. So operator is still linked to origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha. We need to release operator from those before we can assign to schedule candidate. There's release_operator_resource action.)
(Thus after we dispatched origin and destination, we should release operator from them.)
(Similarly we need to release skill certificate and compliance certificate (we haven't assigned them yet to origin/destination; we only assigned operator). So we need to release operator from origin and destination availabilities.)
(Thus after executing dispatch for origin and destination, we should release operator_resource from them.)
(Thus after step 17 (execute_origin_dispatch), we can do release_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha.)
(After step 20 (execute_destination_dispatch), release_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha.)
(Now operator becomes available.)
(Now we also need to release skill certificate and compliance certificate after each schedule candidate.)
(Now we need to load container onto leg for each schedule candidate.)
(We have loading_container_alpha and loading_container_beta available initially.)
(We need to load container onto leg for each candidate. However note that loading_container_leg_linked is set by load_container_onto_leg. After we load container_alpha, loading_container_alpha becomes loaded and leg linked. Then we load container_beta, loading_container_beta becomes loaded and leg linked. The leg can have multiple containers linked? Possibly yes.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not loaded any container before we start schedule candidates; none loaded.)
