(Now we need to ensure we have not set candidate_staged_for_loading etc.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set candidate_loading_verified etc.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set candidate_clearance_established etc.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set dispatch_allocated for schedule candidates yet.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set candidate_dispatch_slot_linked for schedule candidates yet.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set candidate_vehicle_linked for schedule candidates yet.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set cargo_available? We haven't used cargo; it's still available.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block loading container onto leg: requires loading_container_available (the specific container) and not loading_container_loaded. After we load container_alpha, loading_container_alpha becomes not available and loaded. For container_beta, still available and not loaded. So fine.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block stage_schedule_candidate: requires not candidate_staged_for_loading. After we stage, it becomes true; we will not stage again.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block verify_loading_profile_nominal: requires not candidate_loading_verified. After we verify, it becomes true.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block establish_clearance_nominal: requires not candidate_clearance_established. After we establish, it becomes true.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block finalize_candidate_direct: requires not candidate_finalized. After we finalize, it becomes true.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate: requires not dispatch_allocated ?candidate. After we allocate, it becomes true; after execute_schedule_dispatch, dispatch_allocated remains true, but we will not allocate again for same candidate.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block execute_schedule_dispatch: requires not dispatched ?candidate. After we dispatch, it becomes true; we won't try again.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block release_skill_certificate: requires candidate_skill_certificate_linked. After we assign skill certificate, we have that linked; we can release.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block release_compliance_certificate: requires candidate_compliance_certificate_linked.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block release_operator_resource: requires candidate_operator_linked.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block detach_task_profile: requires candidate_task_profile_linked.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not set any predicates that block attach_task_profile for second candidate: requires route_task_profile_available. After we detach)
